  "verbalization": "Acitretin, a retinoid derivative, is consistently linked to Rxrb through multiple pathways in the hetionet dataset. The evidence suggests that Acitretin, as a member of the retinoid family, binds to Rxrb through a shared biological pathway involving retinoic acid agents and carboxylic acids. This is supported by the presence of multiple lowest common ancestors, indicating a common functional or structural relationship between Acitretin and Rxrb across different retinoid compounds. The shared involvement of retinoic acid agents and carboxylic acids in the binding process suggests a mechanistic link that is consistent across different retinoid derivatives. The integration of these pathways implies that Acitretin may exert its effects through a mechanism involving the interaction with Rxrb, potentially through a common intermediate in the retinoid signaling pathway. The evidence is robust and consistent, supporting a direct relationship between Acitretin and Rxrb, mediated by the retinoid family and its associated molecular entities.",
